const FNAD155 = `Everyone likes an interesting news story but ⓐ<u>만약 그것이 완전히 지어낸 것이라면 어떻게 할 것인가</u>? Fake news can be very harmful in that it can make people less informed or even misled. Nevertheless, there have been various fake news reports throughout history. Why have some people written such false information? Let's look into some articles ⓑ<u>그 뒤에 숨겨진 동기를 생각하면서</u>.\n\nAWFUL DISASTER\n(A) Last night, an angry group of rhinoceroses broke down the walls of the cage at the zoo and escaped. (B) These animals ran down the streets and injured hundreds of people. Twelve of the animals are still on the loose. (C) Citizens should stay indoors until further notice. (D)\nNot a single act or incident described above has taken place. (E)\n\n${AD_B}`;
add(R, passage(P, FNAD155, `위 글의 밑줄 친 ⓐ의 우리말을 주어진 <조건>에 알맞게 영작하시오.\n\n<조건>\ncompletely, what, make up을 활용하되 필요할 경우 변형할 것\n\n→ Everyone likes an interesting news story but ______________________?`), 'what if it is completely made up', null, { acceptedAnswers: ['what if it is completely made up?'] });
add(R, passage(P, FNAD155, `위 글의 밑줄 친 우리말 ⓑ와 같은 뜻이 되도록 <보기>의 단어들을 배열할 때, 5번째로 올 단어는?\n\n<보기> the / them / thinking / motives / about / behind / hidden`), '4', ['about', 'behind', 'hidden', 'motives', 'the']);
const HOW142 = `There are many "fake" news articles published every day. As readers, we need to read critically and judge whether the news is real or fake.\n\nHow to spot fake news!\nⓐ________ the Source\n• Is it from a ⓑ________ source?\n• Can we ⓒ________ the writer?\nCHECK the Date\n• Is it a new or an old story?\n• Is it related to ⓓ________ events?\nREAD BEYOND the Headlines\n• Does the headline ⓔ________ the content?`;
add(R, passage(P, HOW142, `위 글의 빈칸 ⓐ~ⓔ에 들어갈 말로 알맞지 않은 것은?`), '2', ['ⓐ: consider', 'ⓑ: release', 'ⓒ: trust', 'ⓓ: current', 'ⓔ: match']);
