add(R, `다음 글을 읽고 답할 수 없는 질문은?\n\nLast night, an angry group of rhinoceroses broke down the walls of the cage at the zoo and escaped. They also broke down the walls of the other wild animals' cages. These animals ran down the streets and injured hundreds of people. Twelve of the animals are still on the loose. Citizens should stay indoors until further notice.`, '4', ['What did citizens have to do?', 'How many people got injured?', 'How many animals are still free?', 'What made rhinoceroses get angry?', 'What broke down the walls of the cage at the zoo at first?']);
const ABC144 = `[A] AWFUL DISASTER\nLast night, an angry group of rhinoceroses broke down the walls of the cage at the zoo and escaped. They also broke down the walls of the other cages. These animals ran down the streets and injured hundreds of people. Twelve of the animals are still on the loose. Citizens should stay indoors until further notice.\nThe Herald   November 9th, 1874\n\n[B]\nAt that time, those who read the article carefully laughed out loud. There was actually a little comment that said 'Not a single act or incident described above has taken place.' at the end of the article below the picture of animals. Those who didn't read it to the end and missed the comment got really worried. Not knowing the news was false, many people panicked. Some tried to escape the city while others went into the parks with guns to hunt the animals.\nSo why did The Herald make up such news? Later, they confessed that they made it up so that they could draw the readers' attention to the unsafe conditions at the zoo.\n\n[C] As readers, we need to read articles critically.\nHow to read articles critically\n(1) Consider the Source\n- Is it from a reliable source?\n- Can we trust the writer?\n(2) Check the Date\n- Is it a new or an old story?\n- Is it related to events happening these days?\n(3) Read Beyond the Headlines\n- Does the headline match the content?\n(4) Find Supporting Sources\n- Do other related stories provide similar content?`;
add(R, passage(P, ABC144, `위 글의 [A]~[C]를 올바르게 이해한 것은?`), '1', ['In [A], the article said that twelve animals have not got caught yet.', 'According to [B], the readers who read the article to the end carefully became really worried.', 'In [A], some animals tried to escape the city when people with guns went into the zoo.', 'The purpose of The Herald was to make people who read the article pay attention to saving wild animals.', 'Four important ways to consider when people write their own articles are mentioned.']);
add(R, passage(P, ABC144, `위 글의 [C]의 (1)~(4)의 기준을 적용하여 [A] 기사를 비판적으로 읽지 않은 사람은?`), '4', ['재은: The article was written by The Herald, a famous and trusted newspaper company. We could trust the source.', "현덕: The article was published in 1874. It means that it is such an old story. Plus, I haven't heard of any related current incident on TV or on the Internet.", "은주: When I take a look at the article's headline 'AWFUL DISASTER', it fits the story about the animals on the loose.", '은명: I thought about the main purpose of the article. I think that it wanted the citizens to stay indoors until further notice.', '근영: I found out other newspapers published articles about animals that escaped from the zoo in the city center.']);
add(R, `다음 글의 내용과 관련 없는 의견은?\n\n1. Consider the Source\nIs it from a reliable source?\nCan we trust the writer?\n2. Check the Date\nIs it a new or an old story?\nIs it related to current events?\n3. Read Beyond the Headlines\nDoes the headline match the content?\n4. Find Supporting Sources\nDo other related stories provide similar content?`, '4', ['소정: 제목이 기사 내용과 일치하는지가 중요하기 때문에 기사 제목 그 이상을 읽는 것이 가장 중요하다고 생각해.', '현영: 글쓴이를 신뢰할 수 있다면 그 기사를 믿을 수 있기 때문에 기사의 출처를 고려하는 것이 가장 중요하다고 생각해.', '미화: 최신 기사를 읽고 있는지 확인하기 위해 기사 날짜를 체크하는 것이 가장 중요하다고 생각해.', '민숙: 다양한 댓글을 통해 기사의 사실 여부를 판단하려면 다른 사람들의 댓글을 읽어보는 것이 가장 중요하다고 생각해.', '대성: 관련 자료를 통해 기사의 정확성을 확인할 수 있기 때문에 나는 뒷받침하는 자료들을 찾는 것이 가장 중요하다고 생각해.']);
add(R, `다음 글의 밑줄 친 ⓐ~ⓔ 중, 어법상 어색한 것은?\n\nWalk and You'll Get Slim and Strong!\nOur new walking shoes, Wing Walker, ⓐ<u>have</u> various strong points. ⓑ<u>Walked</u> with Wing Walker, you burn more calories and ⓒ<u>get</u> slimmer. They also strengthen leg muscles ⓓ<u>because</u> they use the hidden board technology. ⓔ<u>Upgrade</u> your walking experience with Wing Walker!`, '2', CIRCLE);

// ═════════════ 5회 ═════════════ 어휘 5,11 / 어법 17,27,35,36 / 대화 43,60,61,62,63 / 독해 102,120~122,128,129,132~135,138~141,146~148 / 외 173
n = 0; R = S.R5;
add(R, `다음 문장의 빈칸에 공통으로 들어갈 말로 알맞은 것은?\n\n• I'm looking for a quiet ________ to fish.\n• He put on a white tie with blue ________s.\n• There are a lot of ________s on your window.\n• I ________ed him at once as an American.`, '4', ['line', 'dust', 'point', 'spot', 'source']);
add(R, `다음 영영풀이가 어색한 것은?`, '1', ['disaster: a strong disagreement in talking or discussing something', 'panic: to suddenly fell so worried that you cannot be reasonable', 'mislead: to cause someone to believe something that is not true', 'spot: to see or notice someone or something', 'fake: not real but made to seem real']);
add(R, `다음 주어진 문장과 같은 뜻이 되도록 빈칸 (A), (B)에 들어갈 말이 바르게 연결된 것을 고르면?\n\nRead the book carefully so that you can find hidden ideas.\n→ Read the book carefully (A)________ you can find hidden ideas.\n→ Read the book carefully (B)________ find hidden ideas.`, '4', ['(A) such that – (B) in order that', '(A) so as to – (B) in order to', '(A) such that – (B) order to', '(A) in order that – (B) so as to', '(A) in order that – (B) such that']);
add(R, `다음 <보기>와 같이 문장을 바꿔 쓸 때, 어법상 어색한 것은? (정답 2개)\n\n<보기>\nWhen I arrived home late at night, I saw some fruits and ate them.\n→ Arriving home late at night, I saw some fruits and ate them.`, '3, 5', ['As he felt so excited, he jumped high. → Feeling so excited, he jumped high.', 'Because she was sick, she was absent from school. → Being sick, she was absent from school.', 'As she broke her arm, she is absent from school. → Breaking her arm, she is absent from school.', 'After she went inside the room, she turned the lights on. → Going inside the room, she turned the lights on.', "Since the bakery was closed, I couldn't buy breakfast for the next day. → Being closed, I couldn't buy breakfast for the next day."]);
add(R, `다음 두 문장을 'so that'을 활용하여 어법에 맞게 한 문장으로 만드시오.${FULL}\n\n• She turned off the light.\n• I could get a deep sleep.\n\n→ ______________________________`, 'She turned off the light so that I could get a deep sleep.', null);
add(R, `다음 일기에서 어법상 어색한 두 곳을 찾고, <조건>에 맞게 바르게 고쳐 쓰시오. (단, 어색한 부분이 단어 또는 2단어가 연속된 어구 일 수도 있음)\n\nI usually get up at 7 a.m. Today, I woke up at 8 a.m.! Finish breakfast, I took a taxi to school. Strangely, I couldn't see anyone in the classroom. Not knowing what happened, I called my friend, Sam. He said everyone was at Seoul Land. Right! Today was a field trip day! I felt so embarrassed, I took a taxi again. Luckily, I met all of my classmates at Seoul Land.\n\n<조건>\n어색한 부분을 찾아 분사구문 형태로 표현할 것\n\n(1) 잘못된 부분 → 고친 표현\n(2) 잘못된 부분 → 고친 표현`, 'Finish → Finishing / I felt → Feeling', null, { subParts: sp(['Finish → Finishing', 'I felt → Feeling']) });
add(R, `다음 대화 중 어색한 것은?`, '1', ["A: I think I got a cold because I didn't dress warmly last night. / B: I'm supposed to go see a doctor.", 'A: The article says that a goldfish can see more colors than a human. / B: Can you give me more information about it?', 'A: I think Sarah got a boyfriend during the vacation. / B: What makes you say that?', 'A: Do you think I should buy this engine oil? It is reported that it can protect engines from damage. / B: I will read the print first. Please, wait a second.', "A: People say that the frozen fruits are as fresh as fresh ones. / B: Oh, than I'll take the frozen fruits. It will save me money."]);
add(R, `다음 대화의 밑줄 친 부분의 의미로 알맞은 것은?\n\n${GOLD('W', 'M').replace('M: Why do you say so?', 'M: <u>Why do you say so?</u>')}`, '4', ['Who is wrong?', 'Why are you wrong?', 'Would you tell me about it?', 'What makes you say that?', 'Could you tell me more about it?']);
const NAP61 = NAP('W', 'M').replace('M: Oh, really? Can you tell me more about it?', 'M: Oh, really? ______________________');
add(R, passage(D, NAP61, `위 대화의 빈칸에 들어갈 말로 알맞은 것은?`), '5', ['Did you know that?', 'What do you think?', 'Why do you say that?', 'What makes you think so?', 'Can you tell me more about it?']);
add(R, passage(D, NAP61, `위 대화를 읽고 아래 신문 기사에서 흐름상 어색한 것을 고르면?\n\nDAILY NEWS   May 7th, 2020\nⓐ<u>Was Napoleon Really Short?</u>\nⓑ<u>We have been wrong about Napoleon's height.</u> ⓒ<u>The misunderstanding came from the difference between the French measuring system and the English one.</u> ⓓ<u>An inch in France was shorter than an inch in America.</u> ⓔ<u>He was actually about 168 cm tall!</u>`), '4', CIRCLE);
