add(R, passage(P, SLAV132, `위 글을 읽고 답할 수 없는 것을 고르시오.\n\nWhich CANNOT be answered according to the text?`), '3', ['Why is Swenekafew at the hospital?', 'When and where was Swenekafew shot?', 'Why did The Daily News steal the article?', 'What did Pecitello do after the shooting?', 'Why did The Daily Telegram write the fake news?']);
add(R, passage(P, SLAV135, `위 글의 내용으로 알 수 없는 것은?`), '4', ['The Daily News는 경쟁사의 기사를 베껴 보도했다.', 'The Daily News는 비도덕적 행동으로 대중들에게 비난을 받았다.', 'The Daily Telegram은 슬라브인의 이름에 그들의 행동을 암시했다.', 'Pecitello는 The Daily News의 표절을 밝혀내기 위 위 목적으로 위의 행동을 했다.', 'The Daily Telegram는 The Daily News가 자신들의 기사를 무단 도용한다고 의심해왔다.']);
const AD138 = `AWFUL DISASTER\nLast night, an angry group of rhinoceroses broke down the walls of the cage at the zoo and escaped. They also broke down the walls of the other wild animals' cages. These animals ran down the streets and ⓐ<u>injured</u> hundreds of people. Twelve of the animals are still on the loose. Citizens should stay indoors until further notice.\n*Not a single act or incident ⓑ<u>described</u> above ⓒ<u>has taken place</u>.\n-The Herald, November 9th, 1874\n\nAt that time, those who read the article carefully laughed out loud. Those who didn't read it to the end got really worried. ⓓ<u>Knowing</u> the news was false, many people panicked. (A)__________ tried to escape the city while (B)__________ went into the parks with guns to hunt the animals.\nSo why did The Herald make up such news? Later, they ⓔ<u>confessed</u> that they made it up (C)<u>so that</u> they could draw the readers' attention to the unsafe conditions at the zoo.`;
