const TWO160 = `(article 1) AWFUL DISASTER\nLast night, an angry group of rhinoceroses broke down the walls of the cage at the zoo and escaped. They also broke down the walls of the other wild animals' cages. These animals ran down the streets and injured hundreds of people. Twelve of the animals are still ⓐ<u>on the loose</u>. Citizens should stay indoors ⓑ<u>until further notice</u>.\n*Not a single act or incident described above has ⓒ<u>taken place</u>.\n------------------------------\nAt that time, those who read the article carefully ⓓ<u>laughed out loud</u>. Those who didn't read it to the end got really worried. Not knowing the news was false, many people panicked. Some tried to escape the city while others went into the parks with guns to hunt the animals.\nSo why did The Herald make up such news? Later, they confessed that they made it up so that they could draw the readers' attention to the unsafe conditions at the zoo.\n\n(article 2) SLAV SHOOTS A FRIEND IN ARGUMENT\nThe two men had an argument during a meeting. The argument led to a fight, and Pecitello shot Swenekafew twice, in the chest and leg. He is now at the hospital ⓔ<u>in critical condition</u>. Pecitello ran away after the shooting. The police are searching for him now and are warning citizens that he is extremely dangerous.\n------------------------------\nThe Daily Telegram published this fake article so that they could prove if The Daily News, their competitor, was stealing their articles. The Daily News published the same article about "Swenekafew" the next day and thus got caught stealing. The people at The Daily News had to admit their act and were harshly criticized by the public.`;
add(R, passage(P, TWO160, `위 글의 밑줄 친 ⓐ~ⓔ의 의미가 바르게 연결되지 않은 것은?`), '5', ['ⓐ - 잡히지 않은', 'ⓑ - 추후 안내 시까지', 'ⓒ - 발생하다', 'ⓓ - 크게 웃었다', 'ⓔ - 중요한 상태로']);
add(R, passage(P, TWO160, `위 글의 두 개의 기사의 공통점으로 알맞은 것은?`), '4', ['경쟁사를 의식하고 쓰여 졌다.', '보도 후, 대중들의 비난을 받았다.', '예상하지 못한 결과를 불러 일으켰다.', '특정한 목적을 위해 쓰인 가짜 뉴스이었다.', '대중에게 즐거움을 주기 위함이 목적이었다.']);
add(R, passage(P, TWO160, `위 글의 내용과 일치하는 것은?`), '5', ['기사 2의 총격 사건은 실제 사건을 기반으로 쓰였다.', '기사 1은 야생동물의 위험성에 대한 독자의 관심을 끌기 위해 쓰였다.', 'The Daily Telegram은 거짓 기사를 보도하여 대중에게 비난받았다.', '기사 1을 끝까지 읽은 사람들은 도시를 탈출하거나 탈출한 동물을 잡으러 나갔다.', 'The Daily Telegram은 The Daily News와 경쟁 관계였다.']);
const SLAV164 = `Mejk Swenekafew, a Slav worker at the Columbia Coal Mine, was shot and seriously wounded by John Pecitello near the mining camp Thursday evening.\nThe two men had an argument during a meeting. The argument led to a fight, and Pecitello shot Swenekafew twice, in the chest and leg. He is now at the hospital in critical condition. Pecitello ran away after the shooting. The police are searching for him now and are warning citizens that he is extremely dangerous.\nThe Daily Telegram   September 19th, 1903\n\nIs there anything strange about the article? Read the Slav's name backwards; it spells we-fake-news." Who wrote this and why?\nThe Daily Telegram published this fake article to prove so that they could prove if The Daily News, their competitor, was stealing their articles. The Daily News published the same article about "Swenekafew" the next day and thus got caught stealing. ______________________________, the people at The Daily News had to admit their act.`;
add(R, passage(P, SLAV164, `위 글의 빈칸에 들어갈 수 있는 것을 모두 고르면? (정답 2개)`), '2, 5', ['Criticizing by the public', 'Harshly criticized by the public', 'Harshly criticizing by the public', 'Be harshly criticized by the public', 'Being harshly criticized by the public']);
add(R, passage(P, SLAV164, `위 글의 내용에 대한 전문가와 뉴스 리포터 사이의 대화이다. 질문에 대한 전문가의 답변 내용이 위 글과 일치하는 것은?\n\nReporter Q1: What was the news about?\nⓐExpert: It was about a man named Peticello, who shot Swenekafew after an argument with him that resulted in a fight.\nReporter Q2: Why is Swenekafew at the hospital?\nⓑExpert: He is now in good condition after being shot.\nReporter Q3: I see. I heard that this article was fake. What is the motive behind the fake article?\nⓒExpert: The Daily News wanted to show their competitor, The daily Telegram, was actually stealing their articles.\nReporter Q4: After the article was first published, what happened next?\nⓓExpert: The Daily Telegram was found to steal the article published by The Daily News.\nReporter Q5: What was the public's reaction to this?\nⓔExpert: They criticized The Daily News harshly and had to admit what they did.`), '1', CIRCLE);
const FNAD166 = `Can you Spot Fake News?\nEvery day we watch, hear, or read interesting news. (A) However, have you ever seriously considered ⓐ<u>whether</u> an article is really true? (B) Everyone likes an interesting news story but what if it is completely made up? (C)\nFake news can be very harmful in that it can make people ⓑ<u>less informed or even misled</u>. (D) Why have some people written such false information? (E) Let's look into some articles thinking about the hidden motives behind ⓒ<u>them</u>.\n\nAWFUL DISASTER\nLast night, an angry group of rhinoceroses broke down the walls of the cage at the zoo and escaped. They also broke down the walls of the other wild animals' cages. These animals ran down the streets and injured hundreds of people. Twelve of the animals are still on the loose. Citizens should stay indoors until further notice.\n(Not a single act or incident ⓓ<u>described above</u> has taken place.)\n\nAt that time, those who read the article carefully laughed out loud. Those who didn't read it to the end got really worried. Not knowing the news was false, many people panicked. Some tried to escape the city while ⓔ<u>others</u> went into the parks with guns to hunt the animals.\nSo why did The Herald make up such news? Later, ⓕ<u>they</u> confessed that they made it up ⓖ<u>so that they could draw</u> the readers' attention to the unsafe conditions at the zoo.`;
add(R, passage(P, FNAD166, `위 글의 (A)~(E) 중, 주어진 문장이 들어갈 알맞은 곳은?\n\nNevertheless, there have been various fake news reports throughout history.`), '4', ABCDE);
add(R, passage(P, FNAD166, `위 글의 내용과 일치하는 것은?`), '5', ['No one in this city believed this article at all.', 'The article said that all the animals were caught in the end.', 'The Herald made up the fake story in order to sell more newspapers.', 'Fake news can be very harmful because it can make people more informed.', 'The people who read the article carefully came to know that the article was not true.']);
add(R, passage(P, FNAD166, `위 글의 밑줄 친 ⓐ~ⓖ에 대한 설명으로 알맞은 것끼리 짝지어진 것은?\n\nCan you Spot Fake News?\nⓐ 명사절을 이끄는 접속사로서 이 문장에서 'have considered'의 목적절을 이끈다.\nⓑ 'informed'는 'less'를 'misled'는 'even'을 꾸며주는 과거 분사들이다.\nⓒ 앞에 있는 'some people'을 가리키는 대명사이다.\nⓓ 앞에 있는 명사를 꾸며주는 과거분사구이다.\nⓔ 의미상 'the other'로 바꿔 쓸 수 있다.\nⓕ The Herald를 가리킨다.\nⓖ 'in order to draw'라는 표현으로 바꿀 수 있다.`), '2', ['ⓐ, ⓓ, ⓖ', 'ⓐ, ⓓ, ⓕ, ⓖ', 'ⓑ, ⓒ, ⓓ, ⓔ', 'ⓑ, ⓒ, ⓔ, ⓕ', 'ⓐ, ⓒ, ⓓ, ⓔ, ⓕ, ⓖ']);
add(R, passage(P, SLAV123, `위 글의 빈칸 (B)에 들어갈 말로 알맞은 것은?`), '4', ['got angry that Slav workers went to The Daily News', 'won the 1st prize in the clean media contest', 'helped the police to search for Swenekafew', 'were harshly criticized by the public', "also stole other companies' news"]);
add(R, passage(P, WING, `위 글의 Wing Walker를 신은 효과로 알맞은 것을 모두 고르면? (정답 2개)`), '1, 5', ['날씬해진다.', '다리가 길어 보인다.', '더 많이 걸을 수 있다.', '걷기 속도가 빨라진다.', '다리 근육이 튼튼해진다.']);

